        "5. **Explain:** in one sentence, why can training more of a pretrained network make it worse on 30 images?\n\n"
        "<details><summary>Check your reasoning</summary>The September 2026 grid ran this exact change on its held-out split (so it is a "
        "development observation, not a test result): with the backbone unfrozen at 1e-3 AP and AP50 collapsed to 0.0, and the run took about "
        "4.5× longer (91.3 s against 20.2 s on the reference CPU). A step size that suits a "
        "new head is far too large for COCO-pretrained features; a few dozen gradient steps on 30 drawn images destroy what the backbone knew, "
        "and the head has nothing left to read. With real data you would unfreeze with a much smaller learning rate, and choose on a "
        "validation split, as here.</details>\n\n"
